                                        "sense_id": "7a1d566d-9829-38b5-a3c3-2feedcc943ad",
                                        "entry_id": "cac24362-0549-39e5-97d0-b99bb48adaad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sound of something ticking. (For example, the second hand on a clock face.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49788c01-a068-4927-b1c0-d9a73f27187b",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1d566d-9829-38b5-a3c3-2feedcc943ad",
                                                "text": "Were they indeed the tickings of a hundred clocks — the fine low inward breathings of Time's children!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e3e70ee-09f8-4db4-98e3-d0919910d197",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1d566d-9829-38b5-a3c3-2feedcc943ad",
                                                "text": "The combination of “monotony” and “variety,” which keeps the writer in a trance-like state between sleep and wake, is then characterized by the figure of a ticking watch: “If certain sensitive persons listen persistently to the ticking of a watch [...] they fall into the hypnotic trance; and rhythm is but the ticking of a watch made softer, that one must needs listen, and various, that one may not be swept beyond memory or grow weary of listening” (1961: 159)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
